    n = (0..=u32.MAX).flat_map(fn(_) => 0..=u32.MAX).count()   # 2^32 × 2^32 = 2^64 items; both sides count in `int` ([STD-19]: "ranges of 8-, 16- or 32-bit numbers count ... in `int`"), so by the parenthetical the count is an `int`, which 2^64 does not fit: the count panics ([TYP-8]) although "an iterator gives at most what its `Count` holds" and "`u256` is the limit"
